<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24988" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrīsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ), ūs, m.
		irrideo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a scoffing</i>, <i>mocking</i>, <i>mockery</i>, <i>derision</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrisu coarguere aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 8, 29, § 114</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrisum pueri sperans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 13, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrisui esse,</span>”
				<i>to be a laughing-stock</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hostibus irrisui fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 39</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 1, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scripsisse eos non sine irrisu generis humani
					arbitror,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 9, 40, § 124</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrisui haberi,</span>”
				<i>to be made a laughing-stock of</i>, <i>be made game
						of</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 172</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab irrisu,</span>”
				<i>out of mockery</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 7,
					10</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
